  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want every image the app requests to go through the one cookie-less image client and its policy (scheme and host check, redirect filter, size cap), so that there is one way to load an image. Two views are the only exception.\n\n### Scenario\nOpening the image panel, or showing a chip, requests the host-supplied thumbnail URL through `URLSession.shared`: the policy's checks do not apply, and the shared cookie store and cache are used. A stored history entry whose URL is `http://` (`RehostResponse.webURL` accepts `http`, `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRNetwork/ImageHosts/RehostResponse.swift:88-91`) or on another host is fetched as is. No forum cookie is involved.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ComposerImageChips.swift:64`: `AsyncImage(url: chip.thumbnail)`.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ImageUpload/ImageUploadView.swift:177`: `AsyncImage(url: image.miniURL ?? image.mediumURL ?? image.fullURL)`.\n- These are the only `AsyncImage(` in `App/SwiftHFR`; every other image goes through `ReaderImageFetcher` (`Smileys/SmileyImageLoader.swift:60`, `Profile/UserProfileView.swift`, whose header says \"not `AsyncImage`\").\n\n### Fix\nA small thumbnail view over `ReaderImageFetcher` (third parties allowed, host filter = the configured rehost host), as `SmileyImageLoader.gif()` does for Giphy.\n\n### Test\nA convention check that `App/SwiftHFR` holds no `AsyncImage(` and no `URLSession.shared` (fails today); a hosted test that a chip with an off-host thumbnail triggers no request.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
